cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CookBench: Embodied Cooking Agents in Cooking Simulator"
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite the CookBench paper. Bibliographic details
  are omitted here during anonymous peer review and will be added on camera-ready.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ANONYMOUS/CookBench"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and experiment harness for CookBench, a benchmark for
  long-horizon embodied cooking agents. The agent observes a live Cooking
  Simulator session, plans with an LLM/VLM, and acts through a semantic action
  and skill layer. Includes the baseline mechanisms and prompt-ablation profiles
  used in the main experiments.
keywords:
  - embodied agents
  - long-horizon planning
  - benchmark
  - vision-language models
  - cooking simulator
